cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "scenariocov: scenario-space coverage reporting for a verification campaign that has already run"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/scenariocov"
abstract: >-
  Research-grade tooling that reports which regions of a declared scenario
  space a finished verification campaign never touched: t-way combinatorial
  coverage with every uncovered tuple enumerated, equivalence-class and
  boundary coverage against declared classes, and grid-cell occupancy with the
  discretisation stated as an assumption. A kernel-density gap finder proposes
  the next batch of scenarios with a bootstrap confidence and is benchmarked
  against uniform random and greedy max-min-distance selection; on the bundled
  fixtures it is not separated from the greedy baseline and a deterministic
  coverage-greedy chooser beats all three. Not flight-qualified, not certified,
  not approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - family-names: Acharya
    given-names: Om
keywords:
  - combinatorial testing
  - t-way coverage
  - scenario coverage
  - equivalence partitioning
  - boundary value analysis
  - verification
  - aerospace
